# Hi-hat (#783): Moritz Klein's hi-hat (MKI x ES.EDU) as the ModularHihat
# preset. Six square oscillators through a resonant band-pass, under a VCA
# whose envelope is its supply. The key is TUNE: c4 plays the box as built,
# a higher key a smaller, brighter cymbal. The velocity is the accent.
# The panel: Ctl1 amp, Ctl2 decay (s), Ctl3 tone (0 the band at about 7 kHz,
# 1 at about 4.5 kHz), Ctl4 drive (how hard the VCA clips).
tempo 120
swing 54
scale a minor

# closed: short and bright; open: long and darker; ride: tuned up, ringing
setting closed = Modular ModularHihat: Ctl2 0.05, Ctl3 0.2, Ctl4 0.5
setting open = Modular ModularHihat: Ctl2 0.6, Ctl3 0.6, Ctl4 0.7
setting ride = Modular ModularHihat: Ctl2 0.9, Ctl3 0.4, Ctl4 0.3

track closed synth closed
track open synth open
track ride synth ride

strip closed: Level 0.7, Pan 0.2
strip open: Level 0.6, Pan 0.2, Send2 0.1
strip ride: Level 0.5, Pan -0.3, Send1 0.2

# the accents fall on the off-beats
clip ticks = closed .velocity("0.6 0.6 1 0.6 0.6 0.6 1 0.6")
  "c4 c4 c4 c4 c4 c4 c4 [c4 c4]"
clip opens = open
  "~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ c4"
clip rides = ride .velocity("1 0.6 0.8 0.6")
  "e4 e4 e4 e4"

scene closed 2: ticks
scene open 2: ticks opens
scene ride 4: rides opens
arrange closed open ride open
